<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  iOS-only Info.plist additions, merged into the generated
  gen/apple/myne-mobile_iOS/Info.plist by `tauri ios build` (the generated
  plist is under the gitignored src-tauri/gen/, so this source-controlled
  partial is the regeneration-surviving home — MYND-459 T10).

  NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription: without this key iOS silently blocks any
  connection to a host on the same LAN, so a self-hosting user could not reach a
  Myne sync server on their home/office network (SYNC-46 iOS-only v1, SYNC-26
  self-host). The string is honest and telemetry-free — it names exactly why the
  permission is asked (reaching a self-hosted sync server on the local network),
  consistent with the no-telemetry / no-analytics posture. Myne opens NO other
  local-network sockets and declares no Bonjour service.

  NSFaceIDUsageDescription: required by the biometric quick-unlock provider
  (MYND-329; main repo docs/decisions.md 2026-07-12) — without it iOS denies
  the Face ID evaluation behind the gated Keychain read
  (kSecAccessControlBiometryCurrentSet) and the feature silently fails. The
  string is honest: Face ID only gates the device-local re-unlock key; it never
  replaces the master password and nothing biometric leaves the device.

  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription: required for voice notes (mobile voice-notes
  feature; main repo docs/decisions.md 2026-07-12). The WebView records audio
  via getUserMedia and stores it as an encrypted audio/wav attachment in the
  vault; without this key iOS terminates the app on the first capture. The
  string is honest and telemetry-free: audio is recorded ONLY while the user is
  actively recording a voice note, is encrypted on-device, and is never sent
  anywhere (it syncs end-to-end encrypted like any other attachment).

  NSCameraUsageDescription: required for the "Take Photo" option in the WKWebView
  file picker when attaching an image (MYND-474). Tapping an <input type="file">
  and choosing "Take Photo" opens the camera; without this key iOS TERMINATES the
  app on first camera access (a hard NSInvalidArgumentException crash, not a
  permission prompt). The picker's "Photo Library" option uses PHPicker
  (out-of-process, needs no usage string), so only the camera key is required.
  The string is honest and telemetry-free: the camera is used ONLY while you take
  a photo to attach; the photo is encrypted on-device and never sent anywhere.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Myne connects to a Myne sync server on your local network only if you set one up. It never scans your network or sends any data anywhere else.</string>
	<key>NSFaceIDUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Myne uses Face ID to unlock this vault again quickly after it auto-locks. Your master password is still required after a restart.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Myne uses the microphone only while you record a voice note. Recordings are encrypted on this device and never sent anywhere.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Myne uses the camera only when you take a photo to attach it to a note. Photos are encrypted on this device and never sent anywhere.</string>
	<!-- `myne://` custom URL scheme — the target of the home / lock-screen
	     widgets + Control Center "New note" action (ios-widgets/). Delivered to
	     the WebView by tauri-plugin-deep-link; resolved app-side into an unlock
	     + new-note flow (src/lib/deep-link.ts). Lives HERE (not only in the
	     gitignored gen/apple/project.yml) so a fresh clone's `tauri ios init`
	     keeps it — the same regeneration-surviving channel as the usage strings
	     above (the Android side of the same scheme comes from tauri.conf.json
	     plugins.deep-link, injected into AndroidManifest.xml by the plugin). -->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>md.myne.mobile</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>myne</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
